:: End1 [ending] {"position":"1050,2575","size":"100,100"}
ui.status: true
ui.headerRight: "[[Restart|Start]]"
ui.footerCenter: ""
--

<span class="passage-title">Your legislative period in Phonopolis is over</span>.<br> 
Find out about your achievements in office.<br>
<img src="images/government.webp" class="story-illustration">

[[Continue->End2]]



:: End2 [ending prose] {"position":"100,2375","size":"100,100"}
ui.status: true
ui.headerRight: "[[Restart|Start]]"
ui.footerCenter: ""
--
Here is the state of Phonopolis after your legislative period:
{summary row: "circularity", value: circle, first: true}
[if circle < 4]
Your choices did not really improve the **circularity** of the economy.
[if circle > 3 && circle < 5]
Your choices were not very efficient in building a **circular** economy.
[if circle > 4 && circle < 8]
You have improved the **circularity** of the economy.
[if circle > 7 && circle < 11]
You have improved the **circularity** of the economy significantly.
[if circle > 10]
You improved the **circularity** of the economy tremendously.
[continue]
{end summary row}

{summary row: "happiness", value: happy}
[if happy < 3]
People are not very **happy** with your choices.

[if happy > 2 && happy < 7]
The **happiness** of the people did not change much.

[if happy > 6 && happy < 10]
People are quite **happy** with your choices.

[if happy > 9]
People are very **happy** with your choices.
[continue]
{end summary row}

{summary row: "budget", value: money}
[if money < 2]
You barely managed not to go bankrupt.

[if money > 1 && money < 5]
You have less **money** left than what you started with.

[if money > 4 && money < 6]
You spent as much **money** as you earned.

[if money > 5]
You earned more **money** than you spent.
[continue]
{end summary row}


[if happy > 0]
<div class="passage-navigation">
[[Continue->End3]]
</div>


:: End3 [ending] {"position":"125,1225","size":"100,100"}
final: 2.5*circle + 1.5*happy + money
ui.footerCenter: "[[Credits->End.Credits]]"
ui.status: true
--
<div class="ending-assessment">
[if final > 50]
<img src="images/very-good.png" class="score-icon"> <img src="images/very-good.png" class="score-icon"> <img src="images/very-good.png" class="score-icon"> <br>
**You've hit the high score! Congratulations!**

[if final > 32.7 && final <50.1]
<img src="images/very-good.png" class="score-icon"> <br>
Your score is {final} of 50. <br><br>
You have been an outstanding mayor for Phonopolis. **Congratulations!** 

[if final > 28.7 && final <32.6]
<img src="images/good.png" class="score-icon"> <br>
Your score is {final} of 50. <br><br>
You have been a good mayor for Phonopolis. 

[if final > 22.7 && final <28.6]
<img src="images/neutral.png" class="score-icon"> <br>
Your score is {final} of 50. <br><br>
You have been an avarage mayor for Phonopolis. 

[if final > 14.7 && final <22.6]
<img src="images/bad.png" class="score-icon"> <br>
Your score is {final} of 50. <br><br>
You have been a poor mayor for Phonopolis. 

[if final <14.6 && final >2]
<img src="images/bad.png" class="score-icon"> <br>
Your score is {final} of 50. <br><br>
You barely survived this legislative period in Phonopolis.


[if final > -5]
[[Run for office again|Start]]
</div>

<div class="score-details-link">
[[Learn more about the score->End4]]
</div>


:: End4 [ending prose] {"position":"300,1225","size":"100,100"}
ui.footerCenter: "[[Restart|Start]]       [[Credits->End.Credits]]"
--
The score is calculated from the values for circularity, happiness and your left over budget. 

Score = 2.5 * <img src="images/circularity.webp" class="indicator-icon"> + 1.5 * <img src="images/good.webp" class="indicator-icon indicator-icon-offset-3"> + 1 * <img src="images/money.webp" class="indicator-icon">

With the values from your current game, you reached:<br>
Score = 2.5 * {circle} + 1.5 * {happy} + 1 * {money} = {final}

<div class="passage-navigation">
[[Continue->End5]]
</div>


:: End5 [ending prose] {"position":"475,1225","size":"100,100"}
The game contains many decision points where you choose between different options: Six rounds of <span class="policy">policy</span> decisions, up to three rounds of <span class="tech">technology</span> decisions, and up to three <span class="event">events</span> are possible.

Each sequence of decisions creates a unique path through the game, resulting in a large number of possible playthroughs.

<div class="passage-navigation">
Can you guess the magnitude of that number?
<br><br>
[[Continue->End6]]
</div>


:: End6 [ending] {"position":"650,1225","size":"100,100"}
ui.footerLeft: "Your score: {final}"
--

There are close to <b>4 million (3.824.020)</b> different playthroughs.<br> 
Find out how many there are to reach your score:


<img src="images/graph.webp" class="score-chart">


:: Event1.1 [event] {"position":"1575,450","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">FIRE AT E-WASTE SORTING PLANT</span>

One of the largest recycling plants in Phonopolis is about to burn down.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Put out the fire.->1.1OutFire]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Do nothing.->1.1Fire]]</span>


:: Event1.2 [event] {"position":"1900,450","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">GLOBAL REPAIR PARTS MARKET COLLAPSE</span>

A major supplier of generic spare parts in Phonopolis is about to go bankrupt.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Do nothing.->1.2bankrupt]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Provide financial support.->1.2save]]</span>


:: Event1.3 [event] {"position":"2175,450","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">MINIMALIST TECH MOVEMENT</span>

A global minimalism trend encourages people in Phonopolis to own fewer devices.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Encourage consumer spending.->1.3spending]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Promote the minimalism trend.->1.3minimalism]]</span>


:: Event2.1 [event] {"position":"1650,950","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">NEW PINEAPPLE PHONE</span>

New cell phone model with popular features is about to be launched in Phonopolis.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Do nothing.->2.1Support]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Promote longer phone use.->2.1Reduce]]</span>


:: Event2.2 [event] {"position":"1925,950","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">PRICE DROP</span>

A technological breakthrough makes new phones extremely cheap in Phonopolis.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Do nothing.->2.2cheap]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Protect repair and reuse.->2.2protect]]</span>


:: Event2.3 [event] {"position":"2225,950","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">GLOBAL CHIP CRISIS</span>

Cell phone production decreases in Phonopolis. New cell phones will get much more expensive.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Support repair and reuse.->2.3RR]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Subsidize new phone purchases.->2.3subsidize]]</span>


:: Event3.1 [event] {"position":"1650,1225","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">TOXIC WASTE</span>

New materials cause toxic waste during recycling.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Continue recycling as usual.->3.1toxic]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Introduce stricter regulations.->3.1regulate]]</span>


:: Event3.2 [event] {"position":"1925,1225","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">FEAR OF DATA THEFT</span>

A viral news story in Phonopolis makes people afraid to give away or recycle old devices.

Your Choice: 

<span class="event">[[Do nothing.->3.2nothing]]</span>

<span class="event">[[Launch a public information campaign.->3.2info]]</span>


:: Event3.3 [event] {"position":"2225,1225","size":"100,100"}
An <span class="event">EVENT</span> happens:<br>
<span class="passage-title">GLOBAL RECESSION</span>

People in Phonopolis have less disposable income.

Your Choice: 

